The development of computer-based facial composite systems in the last two decades further indicates that the limitations of Identikit and Photofit led to the creation of more sophisticated and efficient methods. These systems, such as SketchCop FACETTE, Identi-Kit 2000, FACES, E-FIT, and PortraitPad, likely built upon the lessons learned from the Identikit and Photofit methods, incorporating improvements in technology and methodology to produce more accurate and efficient composites.

