What are the rules and objectives of the card game Canasta, specifically focusing on the winning conditions?
The rules and objectives of the card game Canasta, specifically focusing on the winning conditions, are as follows:

- The game is played by two partnerships with two standard decks of cards, most commonly with four players.
- Players attempt to make melds of seven cards of the same rank.
- The objective is to "go out" by playing all cards in their hand.
- The game ends when a player/team's total score reaches 5,000 or above.
- The team with the highest total score at this point wins.
- A penalty is applied if a team has three red threes and has not yet made any melds, subtracting 300 points from their previous score.
