What is the format of the World Snooker Championship, including the tournament schedule and the number of rounds?
The format of the World Snooker Championship is a knock-out format with 32 players. The tournament is contested over 17 days, ending on the first Monday in May, which is a public holiday in the United Kingdom. 

The format includes:

- The first 12 days of the tournament feature two matches played concurrently.
- The last 5 days (semi-finals and final) feature only one table used.
- The semi-finals are played over 33 frames.
- The final is played over 35 frames.

Prior to 1997, the semi-finals were played over 31 frames.
