These figures are used by cartographers to accurately define the cardinal points and provide a systematic means to record where places are. They are also used in navigation systems, including nautical charts, non-directional beacons (NDB), VHF omnidirectional range (VOR) systems, global-positioning systems (GPS), and similar equipment.
